# Pauli circuits modulo the rules

The Pauli group of circuits: the subgroup `PauliSub n` of circuits modulo
the rules generated by the scalar `-ω` and the circuits `X` (T2) and
`Z` (T3) on each wire.  Section 4.2 lifts symplectic completeness to
completeness through two facts about it:

* it is normal (`pauli_normal`, `PauliNormal.lean`: its normal closure
  `PauliN n` is itself), since every generator conjugates a Pauli to a
  Pauli (Propositions 4.8, 4.9);
* the matrix semantics is injective on it (`pauli_inj`, `PauliInj.lean`),
  since every element is `(-ω)^t ∏ᵢ Xᵢ^{aᵢ} Zᵢ^{bᵢ}` (Lemma 3.11) and
  those are distinct operators.
-/
import QCert.QuditClifford.Symplectic

namespace QCert.QuditClifford

variable (p : ℕ) [hp : Fact p.Prime]

/-- A one-wire circuit on wire `i` of `n` wires. -/
def onWire : (n : ℕ) → Fin n → Circ 1 → Circ n
  | n + 1, ⟨0, _⟩, c => Circuit.pad n c
  | n + 1, ⟨i + 1, h⟩, c => Circuit.shift (onWire n ⟨i, by omega⟩ c)

variable (g : ZMod p)

/-- The generators of the Pauli group on `n` wires: `-ω`, and `X`, `Z` on
each wire. -/
def PauliSet (n : ℕ) : Set (CG p g n) :=
  {x | x = mk p g n negω ∨ ∃ i : Fin n, x = mk p g n (onWire n i (X p)) ∨
    x = mk p g n (onWire n i (Z p))}

variable [OddGen p g]

/-- The Pauli group of circuits modulo the rules. -/
noncomputable def PauliSub (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (CG p g n) := Subgroup.closure (PauliSet p g n)

/-- Its normal closure. -/
noncomputable def PauliN (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (CG p g n) := Subgroup.normalClosure (PauliSet p g n)

instance (n : ℕ) : (PauliN p g n).Normal := Subgroup.normalClosure_normal

end QCert.QuditClifford
